# Marker Podfile — intentionally installs NO pods.
#
# This project is integrated with Swift Package Manager, not CocoaPods. However,
# `@react-native-community/cli` (react-native run-ios, i.e. `npm run ios`) locates
# the iOS project by finding a Podfile and using its directory as the project
# `sourceDir` (see @react-native-community/cli-config-apple getProjectConfig,
# which returns null when no Podfile exists). Without this file you get:
#   TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'automaticPodsInstallation')
#
# Because no `automaticPodsInstallation` is configured and no `pod` is declared,
# the CLI does not run `pod install`; it just builds the SPM-integrated
# AccessCheckoutReactNativeDemo.xcodeproj. Do not add pods here — add native
# dependencies via Swift Package Manager instead.
